+            # CURRENT package/kernel/vyos-1x list on the EXISTING chroot —
+            # unchanged packages are a fast no-op, the delta (new kernel,
+            # vyos-1x, ask-modules, any bumped custom package) is the only
+            # part that really unpacks/configures.
+            #
+            # Trade-off: chroot state can drift over many runs (e.g. a
+            # package dropped from --custom-package is never actively
+            # removed, only left uninstalled-but-unpurged). There is no
+            # automatic periodic reset here — if drift is ever suspected,
+            # unset VYOS_PERSIST_CHROOT (or `rm -rf vyos-build/build`) once
+            # to force a clean rebuild.
+            print("I: VYOS_PERSIST_CHROOT=1 — reusing existing chroot, resetting install-packages stage only")
+            cmd("lb clean --binary")
